<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Medical communications"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/scientific-communication/"}>{"Medical communications"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-551"}>{"Publications "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-552"}>{"Medical affairs "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-553"}>{"Education & content "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Map the programme "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-551"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/publication-planning-and-strategy/"}>{"Publication planning & strategy"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/publication-governance-sop-and-steering-committee/"}>{"Publication governance & SOPs"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/scientific-platform-narrative-lexicon/"}>{"Scientific platform & narrative"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/publication-extenders-and-modular-content/"}>{"Publication extenders"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/congress-and-symposium-content/"}>{"Congress & symposium content"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-552"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/medical-affairs-strategy/"}>{"Medical affairs strategy"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/msl-and-field-medical-materials/"}>{"MSL & field medical"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/advisory-board-materials-and-facilitation/"}>{"Advisory boards"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/medical-information-and-standard-response-documents/"}>{"Medical information & SRDs"}</a> <a href={"/services/scientific-communication/kol-mapping-and-insight-reporting/"}>{"KOL mapping & insights"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-553"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/continuing-medical-education-cme-content-development/"}>{"CME content development"}</a> <a href={"/services/data-analytics-machine-learning/thought-leadership-content-editorial-design/"}>{"Thought leadership"}</a> <a href={"/services/marketing-communication-content-development-service/"}>{"Marketing communication"}</a> <a href={"/services/patient-education-content/"}>{"Patient education content"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/scientific-communication/"}>{"Medical communications"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Patient Education Content Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Patient Education Content Service"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"A leaflet written several grades above the people reading it has obtained a signature rather than understanding, and that is an ethical problem rather than a stylistic one. So the first number on this page is a target: "}<b>{"grade 5 to 6"}</b>{", which is what the AHRQ Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit recommends for material intended to be widely understood — and we measure against it with SMOG and Flesch–Kincaid rather than asserting that something is in plain language. Naming all three instruments without ever stating a target grade is the weakest possible version of the claim, and it is the usual one. Grade your own material below, then read what the packages actually contain. Pubrica’s patient education writers write to the reading level you need, with the evidence behind each claim shown."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#pe-read"}>{"Grade your own leaflet"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-pe"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pe"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One leaflet at a glance"}</b>{" · before and after"}</span> <span>{"Grade 13 → grade 6"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Reading grade, as received"}</b><span>{"13.1"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "92%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Reading grade, as delivered"}</b><span>{"6.0"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "42%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Average sentence length"}</b><span>{"31 → 14 words"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Clinical terms replaced or explained"}</b><span>{"19"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"“What do I do now” answered"}</b><span>{"In the first 60 words"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Clinical text"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" audience "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" rewrite "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" measure "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" clinical check "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"leaflet"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every piece"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Target grade agreed first"}</li> <li>{"Measured, not asserted"}</li> <li>{"Action in the opening lines"}</li> <li>{"Clinically reviewed"}</li> <li>{"Version and review date on it"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $190"}</b><span>{"One leaflet, measured to grade, in 3–5 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Grade 5–6"}</b><span>{"The AHRQ recommendation, and what we measure against"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"SMOG · Flesch–Kincaid · PEMAT"}</b><span>{"With the score reported, not the claim"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we write"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Ten kinds of patient-facing material."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"All of it measured against a target grade, all of it clinically reviewed by somebody who did not write it, and all of it carrying a version number and a review date so the next person knows what they inherited."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Condition and treatment explainers"}</b> <span>{"What this is, what happens next, and what the patient does now — in that order, because the third question is the one they came with and the one most leaflets answer last. Written for somebody who is anxious and reading on a phone rather than for somebody at a desk."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Hospital discharge instructions"}</b> <span>{"The highest-consequence document on this list. What to do, what to watch for, what is normal, what is not, who to ring and when — with the red flags in the first half rather than buried under wound care. Written to be read once, in a corridor, by somebody who has not slept."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Pre- and post-operative material"}</b> <span>{"Preparation instructions where getting one detail wrong cancels an operation, and recovery material that sets expectations honestly — including the bad days, because a leaflet that only describes the good recovery makes a normal difficult week feel like a complication."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Medication information and adherence tools"}</b> <span>{"How to take it, what to do about a missed dose, what to expect, what would mean stopping and ringing. Written without abbreviations — no BD, no PRN, no OD, which is dangerous in a patient-facing document as well as an unfamiliar one — and with the timing expressed as a daily routine rather than as a frequency."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Chronic disease self-management guides"}</b> <span>{"Longer material for a reader who will return to it over years, which changes the design: findable sections, a contents page that works, and content organised around the decisions a patient makes rather than around the pathophysiology."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Clinical trial participant information"}</b> <span>{"Participant information sheets and consent documents, written to the ethics committee’s format and measured against the grade they specify. The commonest reason a submission comes back, and covered end to end alongside the protocol on our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"} data-nav={""}>{"research proposal"}</a>{" page."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Device and diagnostic instructions for use"}</b> <span>{"Patient-facing instructions for devices used at home, where the regulatory requirements in the EU MDR and IVDR apply to the content and the layout, and where usability is a safety question rather than a design preference."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Video scripts and storyboards"}</b> <span>{"Written for the ear rather than the eye, which is a genuinely different discipline: a sentence that reads well can be impossible to follow when heard once. Scored against PEMAT-A/V rather than against a reading formula, because the instrument for audiovisual material is different."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Translation and cultural adaptation"}</b> <span>{"Not substitution. A leaflet translated word for word keeps the source language’s sentence structure and lands several grades harder than the original, so the target-language version is measured in its own right. Cultural adaptation covers what a reader is assumed to know, who they will ask, and what a health system looks like where they live."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Rewriting what you already have"}</b> <span>{"Usually the better first purchase. Most departments have a folder of leaflets written over fifteen years by people who have left, at an average of grade 12, with no version numbers and three different phone numbers. Auditing and rewriting that set is cheaper than commissioning new material and it fixes the thing that is actually wrong."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <nav className={"pagenav"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-who-we-serve-t3lwdc"} aria-current={"true"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-how-it-works-5y2zmm"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-our-experts-ju8ldz"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-sample-work-8d6wlv"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-packages-1tkhnv2"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-guarantee-auul53"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-patient-education-content-faq-11l4d3p"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-who-we-serve-t3lwdc"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions patient material."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of client, and one shared discovery: the folder of leaflets already in use is worse than anybody thought, and nobody owns it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Hospitals and clinics"}</b><span>{"Discharge instructions, procedure information and condition explainers. Usually the request is for new material and usually the better answer is an audit of the fifty leaflets already in circulation, most written years ago by people who have left."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Pharmaceutical and biotech companies"}</b><span>{"Medication information, adherence material and patient support content, where the claims have to be consistent with the labelling and where the regulatory position differs by market."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Medical device and diagnostics manufacturers"}</b><span>{"Instructions for use for devices a patient operates at home, where the EU MDR or IVDR governs content and presentation and usability is a safety requirement rather than a preference."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Clinical research teams and CROs"}</b><span>{"Participant information sheets and consent documents, written to the ethics committee’s format and measured against the grade they specify — the single commonest reason a submission comes back."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Public health authorities and NGOs"}</b><span>{"Campaign and programme material for populations where health literacy is the constraint the programme exists to address, and where translation is a rewrite rather than a substitution."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Digital health platforms"}</b><span>{"In-app content and onboarding, where material has to survive being read on a small screen in fragments, and where it will be updated far more often than print ever is."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Where physicians fit, and why this page sits outside their section"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Individual clinicians rarely commission patient material for themselves — every buyer on the list above is an organisation. But physicians are frequently the people who write it, review it and discover that the departmental folder is at grade 12, which is why this page is linked from the physician writing navigation even though it lives one level up under services."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-how-it-works-5y2zmm"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the grade target is agreed in stage one."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Because it changes the structure, not just the vocabulary. Material written at grade 6 is organised differently from material written at grade 10, and converting between them afterwards is a rewrite."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"The reader, the decision and the target grade"}</h3> <p><b>{"Who reads this, where, in what state, and what they do afterwards."}</b>{" A discharge instruction read in a corridor by somebody who has not slept is a different document from a self-management guide kept in a drawer for five years. The target grade is agreed here — usually 5 or 6 following AHRQ, sometimes higher where an ethics committee or a regulator specifies otherwise."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"The clinical content, settled with you"}</h3> <p><b>{"What must be in it, what must not, and what is locally specific."}</b>{" Red flags, thresholds, contact routes and opening hours are checked against your actual service rather than against a national template — a leaflet telling a patient to ring a number that closes at five is worse than one that tells them to attend."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"Written, with the action at the front"}</h3> <p><b>{"What the reader does now, in the first sixty words."}</b>{" Then what to expect, then the explanation for those who want it. Short sentences carry most of the readability gain, so that is where the work goes; vocabulary substitution alone moves a grade very little and reads patronising when overdone."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Measured, and reported"}</h3> <p><b>{"SMOG and Flesch–Kincaid against the agreed target, with the figures written into the delivery note."}</b>{" PEMAT-P for printable material or PEMAT-A/V for video, scored on understandability and actionability, with both percentages reported — and with the honest note that AHRQ sets no pass mark for PEMAT, so the score is information rather than a certificate."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Clinical review, by somebody who did not write it"}</h3> <p><b>{"Checking that simplification has not changed the clinical meaning."}</b>{" This is the risk in this work and it is real: a threshold softened, a red flag made reassuring, an absolute turned into a general statement. A clinician reads the plain version against the source and signs it off."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Delivered with a version and a review date"}</h3> <p><b>{"Source files, the measured scores, and a version number and review date printed on the document itself."}</b>{" So the next person to revise it knows what target it was written to, when it was last checked and what instrument measured it — which is the difference between a leaflet that can be maintained and one that gets rewritten from scratch in four years."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Content people learn from has to be right before it is readable."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Educational and patient-facing material is acted on afterwards, often by somebody without the training to catch an error. Fluency is cheap and accuracy is not, and a mistake in a teaching module or a patient leaflet propagates in a way a mistake in a manuscript does not."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Drafting structure and learning objectives a subject expert then rewrites. Finding current guidance and source material. Readability measurement across drafts. Consistency across a module or leaflet set."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Clinical content accepted without a subject expert verifying it against current guidance; assessment items, which need review for bias and construct validity; and anything accredited or patient-facing, where the provider and the sponsor both require named authorship."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders, regulators and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as an integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send us one leaflet you already use."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"We will grade it, mark up the sentences and the terms that are costing you the most, and tell you what a rewrite would involve. Two business days, at no cost. For most departments the honest recommendation that follows is to audit and rewrite the folder you have rather than commission anything new."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The reader"}</b><span>{"Who they are, and what state they are in"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The action"}</b><span>{"What they should do after reading it"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The clinical content"}</b><span>{"Thresholds, red flags and what must be included"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The local detail"}</b><span>{"Numbers, hours, routes — as they actually are"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The target grade"}</b><span>{"Or we will propose one and say why"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The format"}</b><span>{"Print, web, app, or all three"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"The local detail is the line that matters most and the one that goes stale fastest. A leaflet telling somebody to ring a number that closes at five, or to attend a clinic that moved, is actively worse than no leaflet — it converts a patient who would have attended into one who waits. We ask for it as it actually is, and we put a review date on the document so that somebody is prompted to check."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Measure it rather than claim it"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What grade is your material actually written at?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Paste in a leaflet, a discharge instruction or a consent information sheet and see the Flesch–Kincaid grade, the SMOG index and the sentence statistics, with your longest sentences and the clinical words most likely to stop a reader. Everything runs in your browser: nothing is uploaded, nothing is stored, and closing the tab deletes it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"pe-read"} data-tool={"rdb"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"pe-read-body"}>{"Patient material readability grader"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"Two grade formulas, the sentence statistics, your longest sentences and the jargon — against a target you set."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"pe-read-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <label className={"tf tf--wide"}><span>{"Paste your text"}</span><em>{"A paragraph is enough to get a signal. A whole leaflet gives a far more stable SMOG figure, because SMOG was designed for samples of at least thirty sentences."}</em><textarea data-k={"txt"} rows={8}>{"Following your procedure you may experience mild analgesia requirements and localised erythema at the incision site, which is anticipated and does not necessitate intervention unless accompanied by pyrexia or purulent discharge. It is imperative that you monitor the wound daily and contact the department should you observe any deterioration, and you should additionally ensure that you utilise the prescribed topical preparation in order to facilitate optimal healing and minimise the risk of subsequent infection. Prior to discharge a member of the nursing team will demonstrate the dressing technique which you will be required to replicate at home on a twice daily basis."}</textarea></label> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Target reading grade"}</span><em>{"AHRQ recommends grade 5 or 6 for material meant to be widely understood."}</em><input type={"number"} data-k={"target"} value={"6"} step={1} min={3} max={14} /></label> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"Above your target"}</b><span>{"target: grade 6"}</span></div><div className={"tbig tbig--3"}><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}>{"19.9"}</p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"Flesch–Kincaid grade"}</p></div><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}>{"21.2"}</p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"SMOG index "}<b style={{ color: "var(--accent-4)" }}>{"· short sample"}</b></p></div><div className={"tbig__i"}><p className={"tbig__v"}><span className={"tflag tflag--no"}>{"Too high"}</span></p><p className={"tbig__l"}>{"Against grade 6"}</p></div></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Above target."}</b>{" Above the target by enough to matter. A leaflet written several grades above its readers has obtained a signature rather than understanding, and that is an ethical point rather than a stylistic one. Start with the longest sentences listed below, then the jargon."}</p><p><b>{"A caution about the SMOG figure."}</b>{" SMOG was designed for samples of at least 30 sentences and this one has 3. The number above extrapolates and will be less stable than the Flesch–Kincaid grade on a short passage. For a real assessment, grade the whole leaflet rather than a paragraph of it."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"Start here: your longest sentences"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"43 words"}</b><span>{"“It is imperative that you monitor the wound daily and contact the department should you observe any deterioration, and you should additionally ensure that you utilise the prescribed topical preparation in order to facilitate optim…”"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"31 words"}</b><span>{"“Following your procedure you may experience mild analgesia requirements and localised erythema at the incision site, which is anticipated and does not necessitate intervention unless accompanied by pyrexia or purulent discharge.”"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--gap"}><b>{"28 words"}</b><span>{"“Prior to discharge a member of the nursing team will demonstrate the dressing technique which you will be required to replicate at home on a twice daily basis.”"}</span></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"Words your reader may not have"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"analgesia"}</b><span>{"Try: pain relief"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"erythema"}</b><span>{"Try: redness"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"incision"}</b><span>{"Try: cut"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"topical"}</b><span>{"Try: put on the skin"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"utilise"}</b><span>{"Try: use"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"prior to"}</b><span>{"Try: before"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"in order to"}</b><span>{"Try: to"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"monitor"}</b><span>{"Try: check"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"facilitate"}</b><span>{"Try: help"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt trow--flag trow--mid"}><b>{"demonstrate"}</b><span>{"Try: show"}</span></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"The numbers behind it"}</p><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Words"}</b><i>{"102"}</i></div><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Sentences"}</b><i>{"3"}</i></div><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Average sentence length"}</b><i>{"34.0 words"}</i></div><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Words of three or more syllables"}</b><i>{"30 (29%)"}</i></div><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Words of seven letters or more"}</b><i>{"39 (38%)"}</i></div><div className={"trow"}><b>{"Flesch Reading Ease"}</b><i>{"13 — higher is easier; 60–70 is plain English"}</i></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"What these numbers are, and which of them you can cite."}</b>{" Flesch–Kincaid grade = 0.39 × (words per sentence) + 11.8 × (syllables per word) − 15.59. SMOG = 1.0430 × √(polysyllabic words × 30 / sentences) + 3.1291, from McLaughlin 1969; the CDC records that it predicts grade-level difficulty within 1.5 grades in 68% of passages. Syllables are counted by an approximation here, as they are in every implementation of these formulas. "}<b>{"On targets:"}</b>{" the AHRQ Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit is the only current federal source that names a grade, and it says that to ensure wide understanding it is best for materials to be written at the "}<b>{"5th or 6th grade level"}</b>{", noting that the average adult reads at 8th to 9th grade and about a fifth of adults read at 5th grade or below. The "}<b>{"CDC does not currently state a grade-level target"}</b>{" and the "}<b>{"NIH explicitly declines to set one"}</b>{", saying the most important consideration is whether the document communicates clearly — so any page attributing a grade number to either is attributing something they did not say. "}<b>{"PEMAT is a separate instrument"}</b>{", published by AHRQ, scoring understandability and actionability rather than readability, and AHRQ sets no pass mark for it: the widely quoted 70% threshold is a convention from the secondary literature, not a standard. And the CDC’s own caution is worth repeating: readability formulas should be used only alongside other means of assessing whether material works, and pretesting with real members of the audience is the most reliable evaluation there is."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Who actually recommends what, because this is widely misreported"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}><b>{"AHRQ"}</b>{" is the only current federal source that names a grade. Its Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit says that to ensure wide understanding it is best for materials to be written at the 5th or 6th grade level, noting that the average adult reads at 8th to 9th grade and about a fifth of adults read at 5th grade or below. "}<b>{"The CDC does not currently state a grade-level target."}</b>{" Its plain language guidance gives technique instead — aim for an average of twenty words per sentence, limit each sentence to one idea — and it publishes the Clear Communication Index as a separate instrument. "}<b>{"The NIH explicitly declines to set one"}</b>{", saying that readability scores and grade levels are not the be-all and end-all of plain language and that the most important consideration is whether the document communicates its message clearly. So “the CDC recommends 8th grade” and “the NIH recommends 6th grade” are both attributions to bodies that did not make them, and both are repeated constantly. We cite AHRQ, we set the target with you, and we report the measured score."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-our-experts-ju8ldz"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Scope, judgement, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, the reporting guideline"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"The applicable checklist"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on, and records it so somebody else could find it again. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}> <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, ICH E9"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-sample-work-8d6wlv"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"One discharge instruction, before and after."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Grade 13.1 to grade 6.0, with the clinical meaning unchanged — which is the part that takes the work. Use the tabs to see the rewrite, what was nearly lost in it, and the scores as reported. Then open the full before-and-after below to read both versions in full on this page."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Discharge instruction · rewrite"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"Grade 13.1 → grade 6.0 · 412 words → 268"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"The rewrite · what nearly got lost · the scores · what is on the page"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the rewrite"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pe-t1"} aria-controls={"pe-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"The rewrite"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pe-t2"} aria-controls={"pe-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Nearly lost"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pe-t3"} aria-controls={"pe-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"The scores"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pe-t4"} aria-controls={"pe-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"On the page"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pe-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pe-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"1"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The action moved to the top"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"The original opened with four sentences of explanation and reached “ring us if…” on page two. The rewrite answers “what do I do now” in the first sixty words, because that is the question the reader arrived with."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"2"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Sentences split — 31 words average to 14"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Sentence length carries most of the weight in both formulas, and splitting long sentences moves the grade far more than substituting words. It is also what makes text readable when somebody is tired."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"3"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"19 clinical terms replaced or explained"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“Erythema” became redness, “pyrexia” a fever, “purulent discharge” thick or smelly fluid. Three terms were kept and explained once, because the patient will hear them in clinic and will be worse off not knowing them."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"4"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Every abbreviation removed"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"BD, PRN and OD all gone. Dosing is written as a routine — “morning and evening” — rather than as a frequency, because that is how somebody actually takes a tablet."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"5"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Red flags given their own box"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Four specific things, each with what to do about it and which number to ring at which time. The original had them inside a paragraph about wound care."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"6"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"412 words down to 268"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Nothing clinical was removed. What went was hedging, repetition and the explanation of why the department does things the way it does."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"Grade 13.1 → 6.0"}</span><span>{"Clinical meaning unchanged"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pe-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pe-t2"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A threshold softened in the first draft"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“A temperature above 38°C” had become “if you feel feverish”, which is more readable and clinically different: people feel feverish at 37.2 and not at 38.4. Restored to the number, with “use a thermometer if you have one” added."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"An absolute turned into a general statement"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“Do not drive for 48 hours” had become “avoid driving until you feel ready”. The first is an instruction with an insurance consequence; the second is advice. Restored."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"A red flag made reassuring"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“Bleeding that soaks through a dressing” had become “some bleeding is normal” — which is true, and it is not what the sentence was for. Both statements now appear, in that order, with the red flag first."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Caught by clinical review, not by the writer"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"All three were introduced while simplifying and none was visible to the person who wrote them. This is why the plain version is read against the source by a clinician who did not write it, and why we will not sell a rewrite without that step."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"3 clinical changes, all reverted"}</span><span>{"Introduced by simplification, not by carelessness"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pe-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pe-t3"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Flesch–Kincaid grade"}</dt><dd>{"13.1 before, 6.0 after. The figure most people know, and the one calibrated to partial comprehension rather than full."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"SMOG index"}</dt><dd>{"14.6 before, 7.4 after. Runs one to two grades higher than Flesch–Kincaid on the same text, which is the conservative direction and the reason health literacy work tends to prefer it."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Flesch Reading Ease"}</dt><dd>{"28 before, 74 after. Higher is easier; 60 to 70 is plain English."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Average sentence length"}</dt><dd>{"31 words before, 14 after. The single biggest driver of the change."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"PEMAT-P understandability"}</dt><dd>{"Scored and reported as a percentage. AHRQ sets no pass mark, so we report the number and say so — the 70% threshold quoted everywhere is a convention from the secondary literature rather than an AHRQ standard."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"PEMAT-P actionability"}</dt><dd>{"Scored separately, because understandability and actionability are different domains and a leaflet can be clear and still leave a reader unsure what to do."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What the numbers do not tell you"}</dt><dd>{"Whether it works. The CDC’s own guidance is that formulas should be used alongside other assessment, and that testing with real members of the audience is the most reliable check. Where a client will run that, we build the material to be tested."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pe-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pe-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Version number and date"}</dt><dd>{"On the document, not in a file name. A leaflet without one cannot be audited and cannot be safely revised."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Review date"}</dt><dd>{"Printed, so somebody is prompted. Most of the harm in patient material comes from content that was correct when written."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The target grade, and the instrument"}</dt><dd>{"Recorded on the delivery note so the next editor knows what standard to hold rather than guessing."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Local contact detail"}</dt><dd>{"Numbers and hours as they actually are, checked with the service. A number that closes at five, given to somebody at seven, converts a patient who would have attended into one who waits."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Source files"}</dt><dd>{"Editable, so the department can change a phone number in ten minutes rather than commissioning a reprint."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What is deliberately not on it"}</dt><dd>{"A logo-heavy header taking the top third of page one, which is where the action should be."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · procedure and service details changed"}</span><span>{"Before and after, as delivered"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Grade 13 to grade 6, and the interesting tab is the second one. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each."}</b></p> <p><b>{"Three clinical changes were introduced by the simplification itself."}</b>{" A temperature threshold became “if you feel feverish”. A 48-hour driving instruction became advice. A red flag about bleeding became reassurance that some bleeding is normal. Every one is more readable, every one is clinically different, and none was visible to the person who wrote them."}</p> <p><b>{"That is the actual risk in this work"}</b>{", and it is why a clinician who did not write the plain version reads it against the source before anything is delivered. A readability score cannot detect it — the softened version scores "}<i>{"better"}</i>{" — which is exactly why a measured grade is necessary and nowhere near sufficient."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Action in the first sixty words"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Because that is the question the reader arrived with."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Sentence length does most of the work"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"31 words to 14, which moved the grade further than vocabulary did."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Clinical review against the source"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Which caught three meaning changes a score cannot."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Scores reported, not asserted"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the instrument named and the target recorded."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Send us one leaflet you already use and you get it graded and marked up, with the sentences and terms costing you the most, at no cost."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-pe"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pe"}>{"Read both versions in full"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-pe"}> <span><b>{"Read both versions in full"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the original, the rewrite, the clinical review findings and the reported scores"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-pe"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Patient education · sample rewrite"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Discharge instruction: original and rewrite"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A composite built from real work. The procedure, the service, the thresholds and the contact details have been changed; the structure of the rewrite and the clinical review findings are as delivered. Ask us and we will do this with one of your own leaflets at no cost."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"As received — grade 13.1, 412 words"}</h4> <p><i>{"“Following your procedure you may experience mild analgesia requirements and localised erythema at the incision site, which is anticipated and does not necessitate intervention unless accompanied by pyrexia or purulent discharge. It is imperative that you monitor the wound on a daily basis and contact the department should you observe any deterioration, and you should additionally ensure that you utilise the prescribed topical preparation in order to facilitate optimal healing and minimise the risk of subsequent infection."}</i></p> <p><i>{"Prior to discharge a member of the nursing team will demonstrate the dressing technique which you will be required to replicate at home on a twice daily basis. Analgesia has been prescribed PRN and should be taken in accordance with the instructions provided; the antibiotic course is BD and must be completed in its entirety irrespective of symptomatic improvement. It is advisable to avoid driving until you feel that you have recovered sufficiently…”"}</i></p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Nothing here is wrong. It is accurate, it is complete, and it was written by somebody who knows the subject. It is also written at roughly the level of a first-year undergraduate textbook, for a reader who has just had an operation and has not slept, and it does not answer “what do I do now” until page two."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"As delivered — grade 6.0, 268 words"}</h4> <p><b>{"What to do today"}</b></p> <p><i>{"“Take your painkillers as the label says, even if the pain is not bad yet. It is easier to keep pain away than to get rid of it."}</i></p> <p><i>{"Take all of your antibiotic tablets — one in the morning and one in the evening — until they are finished. Finish them even if you feel completely better. Stopping early can let the infection come back."}</i></p> <p><i>{"Leave the dressing dry for 48 hours. Do not drive for 48 hours. Your insurance may not cover you if you do."}</i></p> <p><b>{"Ring us straight away if any of these happen"}</b></p> <p><i>{"— Your temperature goes above 38°C. Use a thermometer if you have one."}</i><br /> <i>{"— Bleeding soaks through the dressing."}</i><br /> <i>{"— The cut becomes more red, more swollen or more painful after the third day."}</i><br /> <i>{"— Thick or smelly fluid comes from the cut."}</i></p> <p><i>{"Ring [number], 8am to 8pm, seven days. Outside those hours ring [number] or go to your nearest emergency department."}</i></p> <p><b>{"What is normal"}</b></p> <p><i>{"Some redness around the cut in the first two or three days is normal. A small amount of clear or pink fluid is normal. Feeling tired for a week or two is normal."}</i></p> <p><b>{"Changing the dressing"}</b></p> <p><i>{"A nurse will show you how before you go home. Do it twice a day, in the morning and the evening…”"}</i></p> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"The action is in the first sixty words. The red flags have their own heading, are specific, and each says what to do. “What is normal” comes after the red flags rather than before, so that reassurance cannot be read instead of the warning. And the number has its hours next to it."}</p> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"Clinical review findings"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Introduced by the rewrite"}</th><th>{"Why it matters"}</th><th>{"Resolution"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"“A temperature above 38°C” became “if you feel feverish”"}</td><td>{"More readable and clinically different. People feel feverish at 37.2 and often do not at 38.4. The threshold is the threshold."}</td><td>{"Number restored, with “use a thermometer if you have one” added so the instruction is still usable without one."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Do not drive for 48 hours” became “avoid driving until you feel ready”"}</td><td>{"The first is an instruction with an insurance consequence; the second is advice. They are not interchangeable."}</td><td>{"Restored, with the insurance consequence stated in one short sentence."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Bleeding that soaks through a dressing” became “some bleeding is normal”"}</td><td>{"The replacement is true and is not what the original sentence was for. A red flag had become reassurance."}</td><td>{"Both statements now appear, with the red flag first and under its own heading."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Three terms kept rather than replaced"}</td><td>{"The patient will hear them in clinic and is worse off not knowing them."}</td><td>{"Kept and explained once, in brackets, at first use."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"All three meaning changes were introduced while simplifying, by somebody competent, and none was visible to them. A readability formula cannot detect any of it — the softened version scores "}<i>{"better"}</i>{" than the correct one. That is precisely why a measured grade is necessary and nowhere near sufficient, and why the clinical read against the source is not an optional extra on this service."}</p> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Scores as reported"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Measure"}</th><th>{"Before"}</th><th>{"After"}</th><th>{"Note"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Flesch–Kincaid grade"}</td><td>{"13.1"}</td><td>{"6.0"}</td><td>{"Calibrated to partial rather than full comprehension, which is why it reads lower than SMOG on the same text."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"SMOG index"}</td><td>{"14.6"}</td><td>{"7.4"}</td><td>{"Runs one to two grades higher. The CDC records that SMOG predicts grade-level difficulty within 1.5 grades in 68% of passages."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Flesch Reading Ease"}</td><td>{"28"}</td><td>{"74"}</td><td>{"Higher is easier; 60–70 is plain English."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Average sentence length"}</td><td>{"31 words"}</td><td>{"14 words"}</td><td>{"The single biggest driver of the change."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Word count"}</td><td>{"412"}</td><td>{"268"}</td><td>{"No clinical content removed. What went was hedging, repetition and internal justification."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"PEMAT-P understandability"}</td><td>{"—"}</td><td>{"Reported as a percentage"}</td><td>{"AHRQ sets no pass mark. The 70% threshold quoted everywhere is a convention from the secondary literature, not a standard, and we say so rather than presenting it as one."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"PEMAT-P actionability"}</td><td>{"—"}</td><td>{"Reported separately"}</td><td>{"A different domain. Material can be clear and still leave a reader unsure what to do."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"What none of these numbers establishes is whether the leaflet works. The CDC’s own guidance is that readability formulas should be used only alongside other means of assessing effectiveness, and that pretesting with real members of the audience is the most reliable evaluation. Where a client can run that, we build the material so that it can be tested — and where they cannot, we say that the scores are a proxy rather than an answer."}</p> <div className={"fsm__foot"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-patient-education-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-packages-1tkhnv2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, with the piece count and the language cap printed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"And one worth checking on any quote you receive: “more than 20 languages” is often advertised beside packages capped at one, two and three. Both things were true and the pairing was misleading. The caps below are what each package includes; further languages are an addition, quoted per language, and there is no limit but your budget."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"One piece, measured"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Clinics, diagnostic centres and single departments with one leaflet to write or fix"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $190"}</b><span>{"1 piece to 500 words · 1 language · 1 revision"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"3–5 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Target grade agreed first, then measured with SMOG and Flesch–Kincaid"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The action in the first sixty words, and red flags in their own section"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Clinical review by somebody who did not write the plain version"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A single-page PDF layout, plus editable source files"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Version number and review date printed on the document"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: further languages; design; a PEMAT score."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pe"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pe"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Standard"}</span> <h3>{"A small set, designed"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Hospitals, specialty services and wellness centres with a pathway to cover rather than a single leaflet"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $520"}</b><span>{"up to 3 pieces · 2 languages · 1 revision round"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"5–7 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Basic, across up to three linked pieces"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Consistent across the set: one voice, one set of thresholds, one contact route"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Visual formatting for brochure, poster or web"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Second language, measured in its own right rather than translated and assumed"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"PEMAT-P scored and reported on understandability and actionability"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: more languages; video scripts; an audit of your existing folder."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pe"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pe"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Standard"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"A full set, across formats"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Multispecialty hospitals, pharma, device companies, public health bodies and digital health platforms"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $1,140"}</b><span>{"up to 6 pieces · 3 languages · 2 revision rounds"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7–10 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Standard, across up to six pieces"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Integrated visual aids, and layout for print and screen"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Web and app-ready output, structured so it can be updated without a redesign"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Aligned to WHO, NICE, CDC or your regulator’s requirements as applicable"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"A house style guide, so the next fifty leaflets match these six"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Scores and instruments recorded on every delivery note"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Larger programmes, video production and annual refresh cycles are quoted on scope."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pe"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pe"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Additions are quoted alongside any tier: further languages, priced per language and measured in the target language rather than assumed to inherit the source’s grade; an audit of an existing leaflet folder, which for most departments is the better first purchase; video scripts and storyboards, scored against PEMAT-A/V rather than a reading formula; large-print, easy-read and screen-reader versions; illustration and photography direction; and an annual review cycle, because most of the harm in patient material comes from content that was correct when it was written."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What governs this work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four sources that govern this work, and four that do not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A short list of things that actually apply is more useful than a long list that makes a page look governed."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"AHRQ"}>{"AHRQ"}<em>{"grade 5–6"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"AHRQ Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(3rd edition)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The only current federal source naming a grade: to ensure wide understanding it is best for materials to be written at the 5th or 6th grade level, with the context that the average adult reads at 8th to 9th grade and about a fifth read at 5th grade or below. The toolkit also sets out the wider universal-precautions approach — assume any patient may have difficulty, and structure the encounter accordingly — which is a stronger idea than any single number in it."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"PEMAT"}>{"PEMAT"}<em>{"AHRQ · P and A/V"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"PEMAT "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(understandability and actionability, not readability)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Published by AHRQ. PEMAT-P has 24 items for printable material — 17 understandability, 7 actionability — and PEMAT-A/V has 17 for audiovisual. Each item is scored agree or disagree and reported as two separate percentages, because a leaflet can be perfectly clear and still leave a reader unsure what to do. "}<b>{"AHRQ sets no pass mark."}</b>{" The 70% threshold quoted across this industry is a convention from the secondary literature and not an AHRQ standard, and we report the score rather than a verdict."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"CDC"}>{"CDC"}<em>{"plain language"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"CDC plain language guidance "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(technique, not a grade)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The CDC does not currently publish a grade-level target. What it publishes is technique — aim for an average of twenty words per sentence, limit each sentence to one idea — and the Clear Communication Index as a separate scored instrument. It also records that SMOG predicts grade-level difficulty within 1.5 grades in 68% of passages, and cautions that readability formulas should be used only alongside other means of assessing effectiveness, with pretesting on real audience members as the most reliable evaluation."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"EU MDR"}>{"MDR"}<em>{"IVDR · where it applies"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Regulatory requirements "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(only where they actually apply)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Where the material is instructions for use for a device or an in-vitro diagnostic used by a patient, the EU MDR or IVDR governs its content and its presentation, and usability is a safety requirement rather than a design preference. Similarly, participant information for a clinical trial is governed by the ethics committee’s own format and often by a grade they specify. We name these where they apply to your piece and not otherwise."}</p> </div> </div> </div></section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-guarantee-auul53"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Simplifying clinical text carries a specific risk, and the guarantee has to speak to that rather than to turnaround."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"Measured, clinically checked, and dated."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Every piece graded against the target you set, read against the source by a clinician who did not write the plain version, and delivered with a version number and a review date on the document itself."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The score, not the claim"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"SMOG and Flesch–Kincaid reported on the delivery note with the target they were measured against, so the next editor knows what standard to hold rather than guessing."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Clinical meaning checked"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"By somebody who did not write the plain version, against the original. This is the actual risk in this work and it is not an optional extra on any tier."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Editable source files"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"So a phone number can be changed in ten minutes rather than by commissioning a reprint. Most of the harm in patient material is content that was correct when written."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A threshold wrong, a meaning changed, a score misreported — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" A readability score is a proxy and not an answer: the CDC’s own guidance is that formulas should be used alongside other assessment, and that pretesting with real members of the audience is the most reliable evaluation. We cannot run that for you, and where you can we will build the material so it is testable. We will not soften a threshold, an absolute or a red flag to improve a score — the softened version scores "}<i>{"better"}</i>{", which is exactly why the clinical read exists. We will not claim a PEMAT pass mark, because AHRQ does not set one. We will not attribute a grade-level recommendation to the CDC or the NIH, because neither currently makes one. We do not provide medical advice or decide clinical content: the thresholds, the red flags and the instructions are yours, and a named clinician in your organisation signs the final version. And we will not translate a leaflet and assume it inherits the source’s grade — it does not, and a translated document is measured in its own language or not at all."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-patient-education-content-faq-11l4d3p"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Patient education FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Seven questions organisations ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure what grade your material is written at, or where to start with a folder of fifty leaflets? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-0"}><span>{"What reading level should patient education materials be written at?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Grade 5 to 6 if you want a single answer, and that answer comes from AHRQ: its Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit says that to ensure wide understanding it is best for materials to be written at the 5th or 6th grade level, noting that the average adult reads at 8th to 9th grade and about a fifth of adults read at 5th grade or below. That is the only current federal source naming a number. The CDC does not currently state a grade-level target — it gives technique instead, such as averaging twenty words per sentence and limiting each sentence to one idea — and the NIH explicitly declines to set one, saying readability scores are not the be-all and end-all and that what matters is whether the document communicates clearly. So “the CDC recommends 8th grade” and “the NIH recommends 6th grade” are attributions neither body made, and both circulate widely. Where an ethics committee or a regulator specifies a different target, theirs governs."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-1"}><span>{"What is the difference between SMOG and Flesch–Kincaid?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Flesch–Kincaid grade uses average sentence length and average syllables per word. SMOG — the Simple Measure of Gobbledygook, from McLaughlin in 1969 — estimates the years of education needed to understand a passage, based on how many words of three or more syllables it contains. SMOG runs roughly one to two grades higher than Flesch–Kincaid on the same text, which is the conservative direction and the main reason health literacy work tends to prefer it for safety-critical material. The CDC records that SMOG predicts grade-level difficulty within 1.5 grades in 68% of passages. Two practical notes: SMOG was designed for samples of at least thirty sentences, so a figure from a single paragraph extrapolates and should be treated as a signal rather than a measurement; and no formula detects whether the meaning is right, only how hard the words and sentences are. A leaflet that has softened a threshold scores better, not worse."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-2"}><span>{"What is PEMAT, and what counts as a good score?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"The Patient Education Materials Assessment Tool, published by AHRQ. It scores two separate domains — understandability and actionability — and it is not a readability instrument. PEMAT-P covers printable material with 24 items, 17 on understandability and 7 on actionability; PEMAT-A/V covers audiovisual material with 17 items. Each item is scored agree or disagree, some are not applicable, and the result is reported as a percentage per domain. On what counts as good: "}<b>{"AHRQ does not set a threshold."}</b>{" The user’s guide says only that the higher the score, the more understandable or actionable the material. The 70% cut-off quoted almost universally across this industry is a convention that came out of the secondary literature, not an AHRQ standard, and presenting it as one is the kind of small false certainty that this field is full of. We report both percentages and say what drove them."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-3"}><span>{"Does simplifying the language change the clinical meaning?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"It can, and that is the real risk in this work. In the rewrite shown above, three clinical changes were introduced by the simplification itself: a temperature threshold of 38°C became “if you feel feverish”, an instruction not to drive for 48 hours became advice to avoid driving until you feel ready, and a red flag about bleeding soaking through a dressing became reassurance that some bleeding is normal. Every one of those is more readable. Every one is clinically different. And none was visible to the competent person who wrote them. A readability formula cannot detect any of it, because the softened version scores better. The only thing that catches it is a clinician reading the plain version against the source, which is why that step is included on every tier and why we will not sell a rewrite without it. Three categories need particular care: numbers, absolutes and red flags."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-4"}><span>{"We have fifty leaflets already. Where do we start?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"With an audit rather than with new material, which is almost always the honest recommendation and rarely what the enquiry asks for. Grade all fifty, which is quick, and you will typically find three things: an average around grade 11 or 12, no version numbers or review dates anywhere, and three or four different phone numbers across the set because the service moved and only some leaflets were updated. That last one is the most urgent: a leaflet sending a patient to a number that closes at five, read at seven in the evening, converts somebody who would have attended into somebody who waits. From the audit you get a prioritised list — usually the discharge instructions and the red-flag material first, because those carry the consequence — and a much smaller rewrite budget than commissioning fifty new pieces. It also usually reveals that eight of the fifty duplicate each other."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-5"}><span>{"How do you handle translation?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"As a rewrite in the target language, not as a substitution. A leaflet translated word for word keeps the source language’s sentence structure and its grade, and frequently lands harder in the target language than the original did in English — so the translated version is measured in its own right against its own target, which is the step almost nobody does. Beyond the formulas, cultural adaptation covers what a reader is assumed to already know, who they are likely to ask for advice, and what the health system looks like where they live: an instruction to “contact your GP” means nothing in a country with no registered-list primary care. Practical note on packages: the tiers cap the languages included, but there is no limit beyond your budget — further languages are quoted per language. Rather than advertise “more than 20 languages” next to packages capped at one, two and three, this page states the cap in each package and prices further languages separately."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pe-6"}><span>{"How do we know the material actually works?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pe-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Not from a readability score, which is a proxy. The CDC’s own guidance is that formulas should be used only alongside other means of assessing effectiveness, and that pretesting with real members of the audience is the most reliable evaluation there is. Practically, that means showing the draft to eight or ten people from the actual population and asking them to tell you in their own words what they would do next — not whether they liked it, and not whether they understood it, because almost everybody says yes to both. The questions that work are behavioural: what would you do if this happened; when would you ring; what is normal. If they cannot answer, the leaflet has not worked however it scores. That testing is yours to run and it takes an afternoon. Where you can do it, we build the material so it is testable and revise on what you find; where you cannot, we say plainly that the scores are a proxy rather than an answer."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of patient material."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The same clinical facts usually owe several documents, and only one of them is for a patient."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"THE SAME FACTS, OTHER READERS"}</b><em>{"colleagues and committees"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Customized writing"}</b><span>{"The same finding written for a board, a colleague or a journal."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Physician training content"}</b><span>{"The clinician-facing half, and who may accredit it."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"WHERE A COMMITTEE READS IT"}</b><em>{"research participants"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Research proposal and ethics set"}</b><span>{"Participant information and consent, measured to the committee’s target."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/medical-writing/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical and regulatory writing"}</b><span>{"Instructions for use and labelling, where the MDR or IVDR governs."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"THE EVIDENCE UNDERNEATH"}</b><em>{"what the content is built from"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Clinical literature review"}</b><span>{"The evidence base, synthesised and graded."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Literature search and citation"}</b><span>{"Guideline currency checked, and references verified against source."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library, including one written specifically about this."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send us one leaflet you already use."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"We will grade it, mark up the sentences and terms costing you the most, and tell you what a rewrite would involve — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
